<p>Ford Credit Canada issued a A$100 million Eurobond on Wednesday through ABN AMRO Hoare Govett and CIBC Wood Gundy.</p>
<p>The bonds, which mature June 19, 2002, pay a 7.75 percent coupon and carry a 101.715 issue price. Payment date is June 18, 1997 to give a long first coupon.</p>
<p>Landesbank Schleswig-Holstein also issued a A$100 million Eurobond, maturing December 19, 2001, through Toronto-Dominion.</p>
<p>The issue pays a 7.25 percent coupon and carry a 101.20 issue price. Payment date is June 19, 1997</p>
